# Claude Code parses `.claude/**` itself (agent + skill frontmatter, hook and pipeline
# scripts). Pin those files to LF in the WORKING TREE, not just in the repo.
#
# Why this exists: `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) stores LF but checks out
# CRLF, so a file's line endings depend on which tool last wrote it — an accident, not a
# decision. On 2026-07-22 three agents (`openapi-handlers`, `openapi-hooks`,
# `openapi-code-validate`) were silently NOT loading; rewriting them CRLF→LF is what
# brought them back. That is NOT proof CRLF breaks the loader — `openapi-spec-validate`
# is CRLF and loads fine — so treat this as insurance, not a diagnosis: it removes an
# arbitrary per-file variable and, crucially, stops the next `git checkout` from silently
# reverting the working tree and re-breaking a flow. See CLAUDE.md > "When a sub-agent
# silently doesn't load".
.claude/**/*.md text eol=lf
.claude/**/*.mjs text eol=lf
.claude/*.md text eol=lf
